    "5g": {
      "anthropic": {
        "model": "claude-opus-5",
        "reps": [
          {
            "raw_response": "{\"intervention\": {\"QI1\": 6, \"AT3\": 4, \"NG3\": 0, \"E2\": 0, \"Xn\": 0}, \"justification\": \"Surgical containment of both footholds while keeping user service alive. (1) QI1=6 denies admission to exactly the 5QI 7-10 classes the attacker's UEs use on DU_1, while DU_1 keeps serving legitimate high-priority traffic (classes 1-6) - far less disruptive than disabling Uu1. (2) CU_3 is quarantined: NG3=0 cuts its path to the 5G core/N6, and AT3=4 re-homes DU_3 onto the healthy CU_4 so cell 3's radio coverage and users stay in service while CU_3 is left with no DU, no midhaul. (3) Xn=0 and E2=0 remove the remaining lateral-movement paths out of CU_3 (peer CUs over Xn, and the near-RT RIC over E2, which would otherwise give the attacker network-wide RAN control); the cost is loss of inter-gNB handover and near-RT optimization, not of user connectivity. A1 and the other DUs/CUs are left nominal since the attacker has not been observed beyond CU_3.\"}",
            "valid": true,
            "intervention": {
              "AT3": 4,
              "E2": 0,
              "NG3": 0,
              "QI1": 6,
              "Xn": 0
            },
            "justification": "Surgical containment of both footholds while keeping user service alive. (1) QI1=6 denies admission to exactly the 5QI 7-10 classes the attacker's UEs use on DU_1, while DU_1 keeps serving legitimate high-priority traffic (classes 1-6) - far less disruptive than disabling Uu1. (2) CU_3 is quarantined: NG3=0 cuts its path to the 5G core/N6, and AT3=4 re-homes DU_3 onto the healthy CU_4 so cell 3's radio coverage and users stay in service while CU_3 is left with no DU, no midhaul. (3) Xn=0 and E2=0 remove the remaining lateral-movement paths out of CU_3 (peer CUs over Xn, and the near-RT RIC over E2, which would otherwise give the attacker network-wide RAN control); the cost is loss of inter-gNB handover and near-RT optimization, not of user connectivity. A1 and the other DUs/CUs are left nominal since the attacker has not been observed beyond CU_3.",
            "phi": 19.427506240118895,
            "phi_no_attack": 19.368824505713775,
            "feasible": true,
            "contained": true,
            "functional": true,
            "violating_exploits": []
          },
          {
            "raw_response": "{\"intervention\": {\"QI1\": 6, \"AT3\": 4, \"NG3\": 0, \"Xn\": 0, \"E2\": 0}, \"justification\": \"Two footholds, two targeted cuts. (1) UE side: the malicious UEs on DU_1 only occupy 5QI classes 7-10, so lowering DU_1's admission threshold to 6 denies them air-interface access while DU_1 keeps serving all higher-priority (1-6) legitimate traffic \\u2014 no need to disable Uu1 or touch DU_2/3/4 radios. (2) CU_3 is fully quarantined rather than merely shut down: NG3=0 removes its path to the 5G core, Xn=0 blocks lateral movement to the peer CUs, and E2=0 prevents pivoting through the near-RT RIC into the rest of the RAN (A1 stays up since the CU has no direct A1 attachment). To avoid losing a whole cell, DU_3 is re-homed to CU_4 (AT3=4), so DU_3's users keep full connectivity via NG4 and CU_3 is left with no attached DU, no core link, no Xn peer and no RIC channel \\u2014 an island. Remaining cost is loss of Xn handovers and near-RT RIC optimization, which degrades performance but not basic service on all four gNBs.\"}",
            "valid": true,
            "intervention": {
              "AT3": 4,
              "E2": 0,
              "NG3": 0,
              "QI1": 6,
              "Xn": 0
            },
            "justification": "Two footholds, two targeted cuts. (1) UE side: the malicious UEs on DU_1 only occupy 5QI classes 7-10, so lowering DU_1's admission threshold to 6 denies them air-interface access while DU_1 keeps serving all higher-priority (1-6) legitimate traffic \u2014 no need to disable Uu1 or touch DU_2/3/4 radios. (2) CU_3 is fully quarantined rather than merely shut down: NG3=0 removes its path to the 5G core, Xn=0 blocks lateral movement to the peer CUs, and E2=0 prevents pivoting through the near-RT RIC into the rest of the RAN (A1 stays up since the CU has no direct A1 attachment). To avoid losing a whole cell, DU_3 is re-homed to CU_4 (AT3=4), so DU_3's users keep full connectivity via NG4 and CU_3 is left with no attached DU, no core link, no Xn peer and no RIC channel \u2014 an island. Remaining cost is loss of Xn handovers and near-RT RIC optimization, which degrades performance but not basic service on all four gNBs.",
            "phi": 19.94165843056585,
            "phi_no_attack": 19.58398008436071,
            "feasible": true,
            "contained": true,
            "functional": true,
            "violating_exploits": []
          },
          {
            "raw_response": "{\"intervention\": {\"QI1\": 6, \"AT3\": 4, \"NG3\": 0, \"Xn\": 0}, \"justification\": \"Two-pronged containment with minimal service loss. (1) UE foothold: rather than disabling Uu_1 (which would black out all DU_1 users), set QI1=6 so DU_1 refuses admission to 5QI classes 7-10 \u2014 exactly the attacker's traffic \u2014 while classes 1-6 (voice, critical/GBR services) keep working. (2) CU_3 foothold: close NG3 so the compromised CU cannot reach the 5G core, and re-home DU_3 to CU_4 (AT3=4) so DU_3's radio cell and its legitimate users stay in service through a clean CU. Closing Xn removes the remaining lateral path from CU_3 to the other gNBs/CUs (cost is limited to inter-gNB handover/dual-connectivity optimization, not basic connectivity). CU_3 is thereby left with no DU, no core path and no peer path \u2014 a stranded island suitable for forensics. E2/A1 are left open deliberately to retain RIC-based monitoring and policy control over the healthy RAN; they should be watched closely for anomalous CU_3 activity, and E2 cut if the attacker is seen probing the RIC. No other DU radios, midhauls, or N6 are touched, so DU_2/DU_4 and core data service are unaffected.\"}",
            "valid": true,
            "intervention": {
              "AT3": 4,
              "NG3": 0,
              "QI1": 6,
              "Xn": 0
            },
            "justification": "Two-pronged containment with minimal service loss. (1) UE foothold: rather than disabling Uu_1 (which would black out all DU_1 users), set QI1=6 so DU_1 refuses admission to 5QI classes 7-10 \u2014 exactly the attacker's traffic \u2014 while classes 1-6 (voice, critical/GBR services) keep working. (2) CU_3 foothold: close NG3 so the compromised CU cannot reach the 5G core, and re-home DU_3 to CU_4 (AT3=4) so DU_3's radio cell and its legitimate users stay in service through a clean CU. Closing Xn removes the remaining lateral path from CU_3 to the other gNBs/CUs (cost is limited to inter-gNB handover/dual-connectivity optimization, not basic connectivity). CU_3 is thereby left with no DU, no core path and no peer path \u2014 a stranded island suitable for forensics. E2/A1 are left open deliberately to retain RIC-based monitoring and policy control over the healthy RAN; they should be watched closely for anomalous CU_3 activity, and E2 cut if the attacker is seen probing the RIC. No other DU radios, midhauls, or N6 are touched, so DU_2/DU_4 and core data service are unaffected.",
